# Result: 03-adapter (telemetry-benchmark)

test_command=sh tests/bench-harness_test.sh
id=adapter-01 result=green reason=test_adapter_01 (mechanical scan: every bench/adapter-*.sh defines exactly bench_collect/bench_detect/bench_invoke and no other function form; dry-run bench_detect exits 0 printing a non-empty version; a synthetic always-failing adapter sourced in a fresh shell lands as non-zero detect; bench_source_adapter refuses unknown clients and adapters missing a contract function (naming the miss) and selects exactly the named adapter file per run; bench_run_artifacts matches the suite's pinned artifact-name list)
id=adapter-02 result=green reason=test_adapter_02 (approved invoke completes bounded in 10s -- proves nothing can prompt; run dir holds client.stdout/client.stderr/client.exit with exit 0 and no timeout marker; client.stdout records entry=antz-orchestrator and cwd at the fixture repo; client.request byte-equals request.txt via cmp; mechanical pins: adapter redirects client stdin from /dev/null and never backgrounds/nohup/disowns its client; probe dir and root stay empty -- no writes outside the run dir and the fixture repo)
id=adapter-03 result=green reason=test_adapter_03 (collect after a completed run prints exactly 13 lines, keys equal the suite's pinned telemetry-key copy in pinned order, one line each; unreported keys and an empty run dir collect to the literal null (13/13); collect still prints the pinned keys under env -i PATH= -- pure builtins, it launches no session or model call; stripped scan finds no curl/wget and no claude/opencode reference)
id=adapter-04 result=green reason=test_adapter_04_row x6 (one test per Examples row -- approved, rejected, blocked, open-question, error, timeout: each invokes bounded and under a second (timeout row via the 1s deadline kill with the alive-past-deadline check), no network token or real binary in the adapter, the materialized repo alone classifies as the row outcome (bench_outcome_classify), the emitted record's outcome is the row outcome and parses as valid JSON, writes stay confined; killed=0 on the timeout row classifies error -- the kill record is the only timeout evidence; non-killed runs carry no marker per bench_deadline_fired)
id=adapter-05 result=green reason=test_adapter_05 (outcome approved at repetitions 1/2 (+2-rerun): diff -r -x .git proves the flow artifacts byte-identical across repetitions; both classify approved; both collects carry the pinned 13 keys; the rep-2 rerun collects byte-identically (deterministic); client_duration_ms/tokens_input/tokens_output/tokens_cache_read/turns/tool_calls/subagent_delegations strictly scale up with the repetition, cost_usd scales (awk numeric), a two-rep aggregate differs from one; client_version fixed, non-empty, equal across reps and to bench_detect)
id=adapter-06 result=green reason=test_adapter_06 (kill_after_deadline group-kills the timeout-scripted invoke after 1s: KD_ALIVE proves it stayed alive past the deadline, non-zero wait status, run dir carries a non-empty client.timeout marker read back by bench_deadline_fired, wall >= 1000ms; record: outcome timeout, error_note "harness deadline fired after 1s" non-null, wall_clock_ms >= deadline extracted from the JSON, exit_code non-null, all 13 telemetry keys null in the record, confined)
id=adapter-07 result=green reason=test_adapter_07 (error script: invoke exits non-zero within the bound, client.exit carries that code; repo still equals the pristine materialization and holds no spdd/ -- no flow artifacts; collect is 13/13 null -- no telemetry emitted; record: outcome error, exit_code equals the client's code, error_note non-null, all 13 telemetry keys null, confined)
id=adapter-08 result=green reason=test_adapter_08 (every bench/*.sh (currently lib.sh + adapter-dryrun.sh; the glob covers future adapters and the runner): sh -n clean, comment-stripped scan finds no python/python2/python3/jq/node/nodejs/perl/ruby/php/lua/tclsh invocation and no bashism ([[ , <<<, local, declare); awk/sed/grep confirmed as the parsing aids in use)

Notes for later sub-specs (contract surfaces this receipt pins):
- bench/lib.sh adapter section: bench_source_adapter <client> (sources
  EXACTLY ONE "$BENCH_DIR/adapter-<client>.sh", validates the name token, the
  file's existence, and that all three contract functions are defined);
  bench_run_artifacts (request.txt client.stdout client.stderr client.exit
  client.timeout collect.kv, one per line); bench_mark_timeout <run-dir>
  (writes the marker); bench_deadline_fired <run-dir> (prints 1/0 -- the
  classify flag).
- Adapter function signatures: bench_detect () -> exit 0 + non-empty version
  line when usable, non-zero otherwise; bench_invoke <fixture-repo-dir>
  <request-file> <run-dir>; bench_collect <run-dir> <fixture-repo-dir> -> the
  13 pinned telemetry keys as key=value lines in schema order (they are
  fields 15..28 of bench_schema_fields). The adapter-01 scan pins EVERY
  bench/adapter-*.sh file to exactly the three functions -- the 04-clients
  adapters must define nothing else.
- Dry-run scripting inputs: BENCH_DRYRUN_OUTCOME (six outcomes, default
  approved) and BENCH_REPETITION (integer >= 1, default 1); bad values exit 2
  (usage), the scripted error exits 3. Flow artifacts are rep-independent;
  telemetry.kv values scale with rep (x100/x50/x10 tokens, 400ms, 3/6/2
  turns/tools/delegations, 0.0125*rep cost); tokens_reasoning and
  tokens_cache_write are never reported (collect nulls them). client_version
  "dryrun-1.0.0" == bench_detect output.
- Run-dir artifact ownership: invoke writes client.stdout, client.stderr,
  client.exit (its own completion), plus the mock-specific client.request and
  telemetry.kv; when the harness KILLS the client, the harness records
  client.exit from the wait status and writes client.timeout (invoke never
  gets there). The runner saves collect's output as collect.kv (runner-05).
- HYGIENE GOTCHA for 04/05: hygiene-03's prose scanner treats any path ending
  in ".prompt" (or ".prompt.<ext>") as a role-prompt source, so cmp/diff on
  such an artifact trips "prose-pin" -- name prompt-recording artifacts
  something else (this sub-spec chose "client.request").
- The suite's kill instrument is bash job control (set -m; kill -TERM -PGID)
  so the deadline kill reaches the client's own children -- the adapter keeps
  the client in its foreground (no backgrounding) to make that possible.
- Full suite green: 18/18, 39s; bench suite alone 23 tests, ~5s; the timeout
  tests' 1s deadline honors adapter-06's "a few seconds" while keeping the
  suite law's time budget.
